WEBVTT

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.130
Let us compare love to Western food.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.240
Love is like a napolitan.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.990
An ordinary dish, but everyone has their own special preferences.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.750
Love is like a rice omelette.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.720
You find yourself captivated by the outer layer of egg,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.230
but you musn't make light of the chicken and rice underneath.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.780
Love is like curry.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.260
It’s almost as if both become sweeter with age.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.010
What a disgusting sight.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.860
Here's today's blood type fortune!

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.570
Type As are number one today.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.460
If you take a little trip, you might close the gap between you and your beloved!

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.730
Where the hell am I supposed to go on a weekday?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.410
Later, dad.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.910
So now you've started talking back to the TV.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.580
Going senile already, huh?

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.560
I wasn't even paying attention to it, cue-ball.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.160
You've got some balls calling your own dad a cue-ball!

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:41.070
Besides, crab for breakfast? Are you serious?

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.510
Crab first thing in the morning is one of life's little nuggets of joy.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.740
How the heck does crab and bread count as a nugget of joy?

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.130
I think I just invented crab bread!

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.080
Oh, it's just you, Arashiyama.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.280
How come you look so disheveled?

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.330
Morning...

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.510
Normally you barely make it on time,

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.580
but you're awful early today.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.150
I was late by a hair yesterday.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.880
I'm gonna be late 'cause the stupid bus caught every red light!

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.270
Well, no shit!

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.430
Maybe I should just give up.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.590
Don't give up, Arashiyama-san. Let's make one last sprint!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.260
Wajima-san...

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.830
Isawa.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:35.510
Here.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:36.890
Mori.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.170
Here.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:38.730
Yamakawa.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:39.680
Present.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.280
Wajima.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:41.700
Here!

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.160
Please be seated.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:44.610
Safe!

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.050
Arashiyama, you're late.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.910
Go stand in the hall until homeroom's over.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.460
No way! That's so not fair!

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.100
Wajima-san was only safe ‘cause the thing’s sorted alphabetically.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:58.360
Our last names are the difference between heaven and hell!

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.060
If my name was Warashiyama, I would have been safe.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.070
Boo-hoo...

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.420
Hoo... what <i>hoo</i>rible luck.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.540
Ba-dum-tish!

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.400
If you won't take this seriously, I'll mark you absent.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.120
Whaaaat!?

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.060
So that's why you got up early today.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.240
That's admirable of you.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:20.850
No, that's not it.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.440
I was up all night finishing this.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.180
Another detective novel, huh?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.720
You can borrow it.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:31.670
So, who's the culprit?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.370
The wife.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:35.920
Nevermind.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.690
Who cares who did it?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.950
It's really good so just read it!

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.800
She's acting like a drunk person.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:13.910
Thank God!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.480
Thank you so much, God!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.030
The next stop is Oya High School.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.880
How cruel!

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.410
Neither God nor the Buddha exist in this world!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.040
Such supreme bliss...

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:45.580
Why must I suffer the torture of ending it with a single push of my finger!?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.170
Here's today's blood type fortune!

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.840
Type As are number one today.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:58.110
If you take a little trip, you might close the gap between you and your beloved!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.890
A true man wouldn't get off of this bus!

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.880
I'll stay on ‘til the bitter end!

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.730
Umm, where are we?

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:14.880
End of the line.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.890
I gained 2 kilos in one day.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.230
Aw, crud! First period's already started.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:24.920
S-Sorry about that.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.380
I uh... dozed off as well.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:32.030
Doesn't the bus just go round 'n round in circles all day?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.160
I thought so too, but I guess not.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:37.660
Our world holds lots of secrets.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.410
Next bus arrives in about... 20 minutes.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.900
Even if we hurried, second period would already be half over.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.420
Sure is nice out.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.900
We don't have gym class today, right?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.310
Kind of a waste being cooped up in the classroom all day.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.970
Why don't we just take the day off?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.950
Just kidding.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.260
You think so?

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.470
Eating ramen after barbecue makes your tummy hurt.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.000
It's a whole new town!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.020
She sure changes gears quickly.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:55.030
Yeah, there are people living outside our tiny little reality too.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:03.530
It's a strangely comforting, but vexing feeling...

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:07.540
Right?

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:09.670
Yeah...

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:20.080
Okay! Let's blaze a trail, Sanada!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:20.940
You sure are excited.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:33.700
Oh, sorry about that.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:37.520
I have two really young siblings, so it's just a habit.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.200
You don't wanna?

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:40.920
Don't be silly!

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.610
There's not a single particle of me that doesn't want to!

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:44.190
But!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:51.460
A high school girl holding hands with just anyone is kind of...

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.770
Well, it's not like I don't get to pick whose hand I hold.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:00.020
I, Hiroyuki Sanada, am truly proud to have been chosen!

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:02.980
Thank you so much for all your support!

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.350
I can't hold on anymore!

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.130
This has exhausted my lifetime's remaining happy reserves!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.340
Hey, there's a river!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:38.720
It's the Tamagawa!

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.430
You think if we follow the river, we can get home?

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:51.030
Yeah, but your legs will be worn down to stumps by then.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.700
We're actually cutting class...

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.060
Don't start regretting it now.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.090
Once in a while doesn't hurt.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:05.200
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.810
School isn't the only important thing in life, right?

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:15.840
But what if I get called into the teacher's lounge tomorrow?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.190
We're partners in crime.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.510
If you get called in, then so will I.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.580
Feels like it's been forever since we played together like this.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:27.840
Yeah...

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:33.380
We used to play all the time as kids.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.210
I wonder why we stopped...

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:38.150
Huh?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.450
You don't remember?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.640
Huh?

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.530
It's ‘cause you said,

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.490
Who wants to play with a stupid girl?

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.260
…remember?

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:54.010
I think I do.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.230
I'm really sorry.

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:58.760
It's not that big of a deal.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.440
I was going to tell you one of these days, anyway.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.550
I'm home.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:13.000
Don't wanna forget that emotional rollercoaster today,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.550
so I guess I oughta put it in my diary.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.360
Umm, today... today, I...

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.190
Today, I skipped school with Arashiyama and we hung out.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.470
Huh? Was that all?

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:33.720
‘Guess I'll read a bit to improve my vocabulary.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.980
I already know the culprit, though.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.860
Let us compare love to drinks.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.140
Love is like a delicious blend...

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.440
Its bitterness can lead to sleepless nights,

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.460
yet it also grants us irresistible comfort and tranquility.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.610
Arashiyama, a cup of cold coffee please.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:53.500
Hmm?

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.240
And it's recipe contains misunderstandings and false assumptions.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.480
Hey, who the heck's Cuprice?

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.800
Did you somehow forget your childhood friend's name!?

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:06.780
J-Just calm down, Arashiyama! I said a cup of cold coff-

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.140
And I said who the heck is that?

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.730
You sure have an old fashioned way of speaking, Sanada-kun.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.080
GET OUT!

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.730
I used to be quite the troublemaker way back when.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.080
Can't sleep...

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.200
I bet it's ‘cause of that.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.560
A little early, but I think I'll visit the potty and call it a night.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.320
It's a ghost!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:58.560
That's awfully considerate of you to muffle your scream like that.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.180
Oh, it's just Takeru.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.960
What are you doing up so late?

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.480
Good little boys go to bed at 9 and get up at 6.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.950
I can't sleep.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:10.020
If I could, why would I go to your stupid room?

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.330
What the heck is <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.990
This is partially your fault too, sis.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.680
Hey, have you seen a bottle of about this size?

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.190
I need it for a project.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.220
Here.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:24.670
Relieves muscle tension and replenishes vital nutrients: Napovitan C!

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:28.330
There should be an empty bottle in there, though...

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.100
It had a pretty wicked taste,

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:35.700
but I didn't wanna waste it, so I drank the rest.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.800
And I'm still wide awake.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:44.150
Half is plenty for me, but for someone your age to down the whole thing...

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.050
But thanks to that, I was able to make a really cool castle.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.090
All right, fine.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.470
How about a half-hour stroll to diffuse all that extra energy?

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.030
Really? For real?

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.540
Is it cool? Totally cool?

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.720
Aren't you just a wee bit excited?

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:04.460
Well, late night to a kid is like evening time for me.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.470
I'll give you a shoulder to cry on.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.690
How come we're going out the back door?

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:19.060
The front door has a chime, so mom would hear us.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.270
What's with the backpack?

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:22.710
Travel preparations.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.560
All the strong monsters come out at night!

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:30.050
Where’s that from? A game or something?

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.510
Safety's about all this town has going for it.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.040
Huh? Seaside's still lit up.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.260
Are they still open?

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:41.030
You don't wanna go near there at night.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.260
Look.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.960
It becomes a hangout for seedy middle-aged guys.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.500
Please don't grow up to be like them.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.760
But they look like they're having fun.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:58.750
When I grow up, mom said I should be a lawyer so I can defend you-

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.350
I'll be just fine, thank you!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.310
Carbonation makes me feel a little warm and fuzzy inside.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:08.480
Wow, the market's almost a ghost town!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.150
Now then, where to?

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.990
He's still awake, huh?

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:19.900
Maybe I'll recruit him as a bodyguard.

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:22.280
Huh? Rats, I forgot my phone.

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:23.500
Hey sis...

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:27.940
Oh, you got something handy in there?

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.900
Looks like nothing but junk.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:31.990
S.S.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.290
Ess ess?

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.370
Here you go.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.320
What am I supposed to do with these?

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:39.260
That's not it?

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:42.610
There's nothing else that looks like S.S., though.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.450
Jeez, I'll get it myself!

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:47.800
S.S. is short for “slingshot”, duh.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.100
How would I know, stupid?

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.350
Go tell them that at the panchinko joint!

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:56.870
The season's over, so I've only got two D.D. left.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.480
D.D.... Dehesa duds, huh?

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.340
I get the idea now.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.550
Grade schoolers are so simple-minded.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.800
I missed! There goes my precious acorn.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.890
Don't you mean D.D.?

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.280
If you pull too hard, it'll break!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:20.900
I swear I can hear people outside...

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.490
All right, who's the dead man?

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.330
Come out and take your licks!

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:33.780
Oh, crap! He's gone from  self-defense to offense.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.820
One word can totally change the meaning!

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.830
If you’d just apologize, he'd probably forgive you.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.200
Those eyes don't give the impression that he'd be willing to talk!

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.220
Yeah, but I think Sanada-kun likes-

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.190
Ah, nevermind.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.800
What'd you say?

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.480
Oh, nothing.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.490
I'll apologize to him next year.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.490
You hungry, Takeru?

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:08.080
Yeah, I guess, now that you mention it.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:10.830
Maybe by the station...

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.570
Nah, I don't wanna teach you bad habits like that.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.090
Well, there <i>is</i> a ramen stand by the station.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:21.220
Wow, this late at night? No way!

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.820
Doesn't take much to amuse you.

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:27.790
I’m so sweepy, my eyes are spinning.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:33.170
Ah, but I wonder if that'll make me fat...

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:37.070
My tummy's telling me a little bit is okay.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.930
Oh, Hotori-chan!

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.180
What are you doing out at this time of night?

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:48.180
Did you just mention a delinquent's name?

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.760
Well, pops?

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.270
N-No, I didn't say anything!

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.440
Just "these noodles are taking a really long time!" is all.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:58.300
See?

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.700
"These noodles are taking a long time...”

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.790
What part of that includes Hotori-chan?

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.330
That was such a lame excuse!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:09.500
Oh good, just my imagination.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.380
Thought I'd almost caught her.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.080
Why the heck is he having ramen!?

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:17.110
Cops should just be chased off with fish cake scraps!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.770
Don't you dare get caught before <i>I</i> find you!

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.730
What, no comeback?

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:30.770
Who am I, Lupin?

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.960
Sis looks pretty upset.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:36.080
Can't hear a thing. Must really not be there.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:41.280
I have a feeling that I'll bust you one of these days.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:51.310
Takeru, maybe I'd like you to become a lawyer after all.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:57.040
I guess convenience stores are the only sure places we could go to, huh?

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:59.020
That's where the youngsters tend to gather.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.250
It's pitch black outside the store!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.780
Yet again, the weirdest things amaze you.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:09.760
Well, it's true that normally you don't go out after dinner.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:13.730
This is a midnight reminder from Yamamura Cameras.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:20.500
Takeru.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.150
It is now the 1st of May.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:30.180
Night Head Radio is brought to you commercial-free by "Amigo Kirihara".

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:33.540
Huh? Midnight, as in zero o'clock?

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:35.260
Yup. That's right.

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:39.210
Zero o'clock?

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:42.060
Zero means nothing, so how can it be a time?

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:42.560
I'm scared!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.030
Just mere seconds ago, it was April 30th,

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:50.220
but now it's May 1st.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:55.120
You've just crossed the gap between yesterday and today.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:58.830
Whaaaat!?

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.550
It was just tomorrow, but now it's today...

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.100
It was just today, but now it's yesterday...

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:12.070
Yup. You've just witnessed firsthand one of the world's secrets.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:18.320
I wonder when it was I first watched the date change.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.430
Wish I had written it down or something.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:35.170
Make sure you put your shoes back by the entrance, or we'll get caught.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.360
Ah, right!

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.720
It was colder out there than I thought.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.880
Since we're cold, we should hop in the bath.

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:47.190
And just cover it with a towel...

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:55.370
Think you can sleep now?

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:57.630
Probably.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:01.490
Hey, sis?

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.200
Hmm?

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.150
You sneak out at night pretty often, don't you?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.130
W-What makes you say that?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.410
You know quite a few tricks to not getting caught.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.380
Today wasn't the first time, was it?

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:20.640
I think you'd make a better prosecutor than a lawyer.

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:52.900
Thank you very maid for coming!

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:57.860
Umm, I figured out who the culprit is.

00:22:58.650 --> 00:23:01.070
Let us compare love to snacks.

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:05.470
I've figured out how to pull off the perfect crime!

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:08.130
Love is like a banana.

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:10.990
With its popularity and abundance of nutrients,

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.970
the banana is the ideal foodstuffs for powering our everyday lives.

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:17.190
Kill the victim by hitting them with a frozen banana.

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:19.230
...and eat it!

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:23.250
Yes... no weapons, only the banana peel remains!

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.740
Then just make it look like they slipped and fell from the banana peel,

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:28.880
and it's the perfect cover up!

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.490
Even the police wouldn't solve the case!

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.880
I wouldn't want to eat a banana I just used to whack someone.

00:23:34.090 --> 00:23:36.390
Ah! W-Well yeah, me neither!

00:23:41.370 --> 00:23:43.390
We live in the 21st century!

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:47.600
Behold the pinnacle of convenience: the fully automatic washer and dryer!

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.850
No need to worry about forgetting to hang wet clothing.

00:23:49.850 --> 00:23:54.520
No fears that your clothes will smell sour!

00:23:54.520 --> 00:23:55.880
BUT WAIT!!!

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:59.740
We still have to fold our clothes and put them away.

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:04.280
It's still yet ages before we can truly call it fully-automatic.

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:06.360
Next time: Eighth Street.

00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:08.320
Full-auto Orchestra.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:10.870
It keeps turning nihilistically.
